## Project description
This project is boilerplate code to implement landing website. 

## Top priorities
<!-- - Do not fix files on the app directory because this project is boilerplate for landing project.
- Do not add page on the app directory because this website has to be had only one page, main page. -->
- If each component has many style constants, export style.ts file on the same directory. For example, if ActionButton/ActionButton.tsx has more than 5 style code in component file, then make ActionButton/style.ts file and export those styles.

## Directory structure
- **app/**: Next.js App Router directory - contains main pages, layouts, and global styles
- **components/**: Reusable UI components
  - ActionButton, Brand, Calendar, Checkbox, CloseButton and other basic UI components
  - Heading (H1, H2, H3), Media, Menu, Modal, Nav and other layout components
  - Photo, Popup, Radio, Skeleton, Table, Textarea, TextInput and other form/data components
- **sections/**: Major page section components
  - Carousel, Contact, Description, Earth, Grid, Hero and other landing page sections
  - HorizontalScroll, Partners, People, Video, Vision and other content sections
- **hocs/**: Higher-Order Components for analytics and tracking features
  - GA Event, Heatmap, Pixel Event, Tag Manager wrappers
- **styles/**: Style-related utilities and configurations
- **public/**: Static asset files
- Root level: Next.js configuration files (next.config.ts, package.json, tsconfig.json, etc.)

## Public assets
- public/brand/logo.png: Brand main logo for every theme scenario.
- public/brand/logo_invert.png: Brand main logo for dark mode theme.
- public/audio: Audio source for background music or sound effects.
- public/font: If necessary, font file will be located.

## Animation
- Use motion/react module for animation. Not framer-motion. motion/react module is newest version of framer-motion.